  "emphasis": {
    "primary": "Control — Increase Damage Taken (Timeshift, Momentum Shift; two enemy rows) and Decrease Damage Given (Timelapse circle)",
    "secondary": "Tank — Decrease Damage Taken (Timelapse self row) and Heal (Cellular Regeneration)",
    "tertiary": "Sand damage (Timeshift 40, Eternity Flux 50, Timelapse 40) and the Momentum Shift self Increase Damage Given",
    "rationale": "Sands of Time is a rank H Tank / Control kit whose nine supported rows split 3 Damage, 2 Increase Damage Taken and one each of Increase Damage Given, Decrease Damage Given, Decrease Damage Taken and Heal. Control is primary because it owns the kit's only two-row tag (Timeshift's 35% IDT lists all four stat types and no element; Momentum Shift's 35% IDT lists Earth/None/Sand/Wind) and the only area debuff (Timelapse's 30% Decrease Damage Given on every enemy in the circle), both of which also amplify or blunt what allies deal and take. Tank is secondary: Timelapse's self Decrease Damage Taken (30%, four stat types, no element) and Cellular Regeneration's static Heal 25 (250 HP per tick for 2 ticks) are the kit's only self rows apart from Momentum Shift's IDG. Damage is tertiary by role even though it reaches three rows and takes the Taiyo-standard +5 route; stun, timecompression and barrier are unsupported and receive nothing."
  },
