  "narrow_kit_exception": null,
  "design_notes": [
    "Node split: Borrowed Hours raises both Momentum Shift rows and Timeshift's IDT, forking into Grinding Sands → Erosion of Eternity (Sand damage) and Brittle with Age → The Inevitable Hour (exposure, 2 rows). Suspended Moment raises the two self rows outside Momentum Shift (Timelapse DDT, Cellular Regeneration heal), forking into Held in Stasis → Timeless Bastion (fortress) and Leaden Seconds → Stilled Hourglass (area suppression). 2 F / 4 H / 4 A; capstones 3 BP deep; any two capstones 5–6 BP.",
    "Calibration: Damage reaches 3 rows (as Taiyo Kami) and takes Taiyo's 2+3 = +5, not the +6 guardrail, as Damage is tertiary. Two-row IDT is held at Taiyo's single-row +7 (2+2+3). Single-row DDT follows Taiyo's 2+3+5 = +10; single-row DDG is 3+5 = +8 because Timelapse delivers it to every enemy in a circle. IDG (one broad row) and Heal are glue only, +5 each (2+3). Capstone secondaries sit below the sibling Hidden Art on the same tag (Stilled Hourglass DDT +2 < Held in Stasis +3).",
    "Row weight: the strongest full builds score 25 (01,02,03,04; 01,02,04,05; 01,02,03,06) against Taiyo Kami's 31 on the same nine-row count; all 14 full allocations are non-dominated and every node appears in one. Lowest-value nodes are Held in Stasis and Leaden Seconds (+3 on one row each), the same shape as Taiyo's Golden Mantle and Ashen Verdict. Lever if the rank H kit reads too conservative: Erosion of Eternity +4 Damage (route +6) or Stilled Hourglass +7 DDG (route +10); both are user-owned.",
    "Matching (getEfficiencyRatio, tags.ts 3477–3510; G15/G16): Timeshift IDT and Timelapse DDG/DDT list four stat types and no element, so they alter every non-pierce hit of those stats or with no element. Momentum Shift IDT (Earth/None/Sand/Wind, no stat filter) reaches same-element and element-less hits only. Momentum Shift IDG ('Highest', no element) reaches element-less hits of any stat plus highest-stat elemental hits. The bloodline IDG passive multiplies the Sand damage rows.",
    "Delivery: cooldown 7 on every jutsu; buffs/debuffs last 2 rounds (2-in-7 uptime). Timelapse (60 AP, range 4, circle on an enemy) carries three rows: Sand damage to everyone inside (friendly fire ALL), DDG on enemies inside and a SELF-targeted DDT. Timeshift and Eternity Flux are 60 AP single hits; Momentum Shift (40 AP) debuffs the target and buffs the caster at once. Cellular Regeneration (40 AP, range 1 ground spiral) carries a SELF-targeted static heal, two 250 HP ticks on the next rounds.",
    "Fourth purchases: Burst → Suspended Moment or Brittle with Age (IDT 39%); Exposure → Suspended Moment or Grinding Sands; Fortress → Borrowed Hours or Leaden Seconds (DDG 33%); Suppression → Borrowed Hours or Held in Stasis (06,07,09,10: DDG 38%, DDT 37%, the strongest pure-Timelapse build). No-capstone hybrids such as 01,02,04,06 and 01,02,06,09 are legal and non-dominated. Four examples because each capstone answers a distinct role: burst, control by exposure, tank, control by area suppression."
  ],
  "risks": [
    "Classification: Sand is the single signature element on all three damage rows and no other of the 95 census kits carries it; whether any non-bloodline jutsu carries Sand is unverified. Under the current resolver a Sand modifier reaches 4 of 9 rows directly; the other 5 fall back to None, which also reaches every non-elemental row the player casts. Assumes the proposed whole-kit classification.",
    "Ally hazard (validator warns): Timelapse row 0 Sand damage is a circle spawn with friendly fire none (= ALL), so allies and the caster standing inside take the hit; Grinding Sands and Erosion of Eternity raise it 40→45. Positioning, not the node, decides. The DDG row is friendly fire ENEMIES and the DDT row is SELF-targeted, so neither Suspended Moment route carries this hazard.",
    "Exposure leakage: The Inevitable Hour puts Timeshift's and Momentum Shift's IDT at 42% for 2 rounds; the debuff amplifies every non-pierce hit that enemy takes from the caster, weapons, normal jutsu and allies. Stacking is on at the pin, so both rows can sit on one target at once (two casts, 60 + 40 AP) and stack with other IDT sources. Not simulated.",
    "Area suppression leakage: Stilled Hourglass puts Decrease Damage Given at 38% on every enemy inside the Timelapse circle for 2 rounds, cutting their damage to the caster's allies as well (four stat types or element-less, pierce excluded). The route is worth more in team battles than one row suggests, which is why it stops at +8 rather than Taiyo's +10; raising it is a user-owned decision.",
    "Broad self rows: Timeless Bastion puts Timelapse's self DDT at 40% for 2 rounds against nearly every non-pierce hit; Borrowed Hours plus The Inevitable Hour put Momentum Shift's IDG at 40%, raising basic attacks, weapons and element-less jutsu while active. Both stack with other DDT/IDG sources (stacking on at the pin); a future normal-tree potency budget is unaudited.",
    "Heal: static heal is ×10 HP per tick, so the +5 route adds 50 HP per tick (600 per cast vs 500 at level 25). Recipient 'self' comes from the captured row's target SELF on an EMPTY_GROUND jutsu, not a combat read; if the engine applies it to the spiral tiles instead, the caster must stand in it from the next round and anyone on the tiles is healed. Healprevent blocks it.",
    "Highest-stat resolution (G16): the Sand damage rows and Momentum Shift's IDG row use 'Highest', resolved through the caster's highestOffence; an undefined value pushes the literal 'Highest', which matches nothing, so the IDG row would reach only element-less hits. Momentum Shift's IDT still matches Sand rows by element; four-stat-type rows are unaffected. Not verified always defined.",
    "No combat simulation: 14/14 non-dominance and row weights are arithmetic, not equal combat strength. Stun, timecompression, the barrier, circle target counts, AP, uptime and delivery were not modelled. Both Suspended Moment routes ride on one 60 AP Timelapse cast; a sealed or prevented cast removes their value for that cycle. Ranked modes skip skill effects."
  ],
